\begin{abstract}
The Adhesion--Cohesion Astrophysical Simulation Engine (ACASE-v9.8) is a manifold-based astrophysical simulation framework integrating multi-catalog astronomical data, baryonic and dark-matter structural modeling, adhesion and cohesion dynamical processes, and invariant-driven cryptographic computation. The engine incorporates Voronoi tessellation, baryonic graph construction, interstellar medium adhesion modeling, gravitational and magnetohydrodynamic cohesion, and encrypted GPU execution. This manuscript presents the formal architecture, mathematical foundations, and computational design of ACASE-v9.8.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
Astrophysical simulations traditionally rely on gravitational solvers, hydrodynamic schemes, and magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) formulations. ACASE-v9.8 extends this paradigm by introducing adhesion physics, manifold-level cryptographic invariants, and homomorphic GPU execution. The engine operates on real astronomical datasets, constructs multi-component cosmic manifolds, and evolves baryonic and dark-matter structures under adhesion--cohesion dynamics.

