\section{Adhesion \& Cohesion Dynamical Cores}
\subsection{Adhesion Engine}
Adhesive forces in the interstellar medium are modeled as:
\[
F_{\text{adhesion}}(r_i) =
\sum_j r_{ij} A_{ij} \frac{r_{ij}}{|r_{ij}|}
\left( 1 - \exp\left(-\frac{|r_{ij}|}{l_0}\right) \right).
\]
This formulation captures ISM surface-tension behavior and filament formation.

\subsection{Cohesion Engine}
Cohesive gravitational and MHD forces are modeled as:
\[
F_{\text{cohesion}}(r_i) =
G m_i \sum_j \frac{m_j r_{ji}}{r_{ji}^3}
+ \text{kernel}(W(r,h)).
\]
This governs gravitational collapse, MHD-driven structure formation, and halo--baryon coupling.

